    "description": "Vintage Textile Mill Bobbins\nWood Bobbin & Paper Pirn Tubes\n5 Items, Mid-20th Century\nThis lot of five vintage textile mill bobbins includes one turned hardwood bobbin and four composite paper pirn tubes with protective metal ferrules. Originating from commercial textile manufacturing, these pieces retain authentic maker stamps and working patina, bundled with a decorative plaid fabric wrap.\nITEMS INCLUDED:\n1.\nHardwood Bobbin\n- Turned wood with slotted base and metal ring\n2.\nAmerican Paper Tube Co. Quill\n- Stamped maker mark, \"MADE IN U.S.A.\", dated 1947\n3.\nTextube Green Tube\n- Stamped markings with green grid pattern and metal ferrule\n4.\nTextube Striped Tube\n- Striped paper pirn with metal ferrule\n5.\nTextube 286 Tube\n- Stamped \"TEXTUBE 286\" with metal end ferrule\nCondition:\nVintage industrial condition with expected signs of mill use. Turned wood bobbin shows surface patina and minor handling marks. Paper composite tubes exhibit light edge wear, surface darkening, and natural metal oxidation on ferrules. All pieces are structurally intact.\nWarehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
